/*Q18. Write a Java program that takes a string from the user and performs the following tasks:
• If the length of the string is odd, eliminate the last character.
• Divide the string into two halves.
• Reverse the first half and the second half separately.
• Combine the reversed halves into a single string.
Input Format:
• The input is a string.
Output Format:
• The output is a string after performing the required operation.

*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
public class ReverseHalves {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        String s = sc.nextLine();
        if (s.length() % 2 != 0) {
            s = s.substring(0, s.length() - 1);   // drop the last character
        }
        int mid = s.length() / 2;
        String first = new StringBuilder(s.substring(0, mid)).reverse().toString();
        String second = new StringBuilder(s.substring(mid)).reverse().toString();
        System.out.println(first + second);
        sc.close();
    }
}
